.TH wall 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
wall \- write to every logged-in user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wall
[\fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wall
reads
.IR file ,
or standard input, and writes it to the terminal of every user logged
in, prefixed with a note saying who it came from.
.SH NOTES
The superuser reaches every terminal, whether or not
.BR mesg (1)
has turned messages off.
.PP
This is what a shutdown script uses to warn people.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR write (1),
.BR mesg (1),
.BR who (1),
.BR shutdown (1)
